.TH JEV\-CLI 1 "September 2026" "jev-cli 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jev\-cli \- ask the Jev System One model probabilistic questions before acting; built for LLM agents and scripts (unofficial)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jev\-cli
.RI [ GLOBAL\ OPTIONS ]
.B predict
.BI \-\-question " TEXT"
.RI [ STATE ]
.RI [ \-\-threshold " T" ]
.br
.B jev\-cli
.RI [ GLOBAL\ OPTIONS ]
.B choose
.BI \-\-question " TEXT"
.BI \-\-option " NAME[=DESC]" ...
.RI [ STATE ]
.RI [ \-\-min\-confidence " C" ]
.br
.B jev\-cli
.RI [ GLOBAL\ OPTIONS ]
.B score
.BI \-\-question " TEXT"
.BI \-\-level " TEXT" ...
.RI [ STATE ]
.br
.B jev\-cli
.RI [ GLOBAL\ OPTIONS ]
.B ask
.IR FILE | \-
.br
.B jev\-cli
.RI [ GLOBAL\ OPTIONS ]
.B models
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jev\-cli
evaluates typed questions against a described situation (the
.IR state )
using the TypeSafe AI System One API (Jev) and returns calibrated
probabilities rather than generated text. It is designed to be called by
LLM agents and shell scripts that need to decide
.I before
acting: predict the probability of an outcome, choose the best of several
paths, or grade a situation against a rubric.
.PP
stdout carries only the answer (a JSON document by default); diagnostics go
to stderr; exit codes are meaningful (see
.BR "EXIT STATUS" ).
This is an unofficial tool, not affiliated with TypeSafe AI.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR predict " (alias: " will )
Answer a yes/no question with the probability of \(lqyes\(rq.
.B \-\-threshold
.I T
makes the command exit 1 when the probability is below
.IR T .
.B \-\-yes
/
.B \-\-no
describe what each outcome means, sharpening calibration.
.TP
.BR choose " (alias: " pick )
Pick one option among several. Each
.B \-\-option
is
.I NAME
or
.IR NAME=DESCRIPTION ;
at least two are required and names must be unique. The answer includes the
chosen option, the full probability distribution, and a confidence.
.B \-\-min\-confidence
.I C
makes the command exit 1 when the confidence is below
.I C
(the model abstains rather than guessing).
.TP
.BR score " (alias: " rate )
Rate the state against ordered rubric levels given with
.B \-\-level
(lowest first; at least two). The answer is a probability-weighted score in
.RI 0 .. N\-1
that can land between levels, plus the per-level distribution and a
confidence.
.TP
.B ask
Read a full request document
.RB { state ,
.BR questions ,
.RB [ model ]}
from
.I FILE
(or stdin with
.BR \- )
and print the full response as JSON. Each question id maps to a typed
question object:
.BR noul
.RB ( instructions ,
optional
.BR criteria
with
.BR true / false
keys),
.BR choice
.RB ( instructions ,
.B criteria
map of option to description-or-null), or
.BR score
.RB ( instructions ,
.B criteria
array of level descriptions).
.B ask
always emits JSON; question order is preserved in the response.
.TP
.B models
List the models available to the account.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-format " json"|"text"
Output format.
.B json
(default) prints a full JSON document;
.B text
prints only the primary answer value on one line (probability, option name,
or score) for shell capture.
.B ask
always prints JSON.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " MODEL"
Model to use. Default:
.BR jev\-latest ,
or
.B TYPESAFE_DEFAULT_MODEL
when set.
.TP
.BI \-\-env\-file " FILE"
Load environment from
.I FILE
instead of
.IR ./.env ;
.B none
disables loading.
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-file " FILE"
Load user configuration from
.I FILE
instead of
.IR ~/.jevcli/jev.conf ;
.B none
disables loading.
.SH STATE INPUT
Every question command takes the situation to evaluate via exactly one of:
.TP
.BI \-\-state " TEXT"
Plain text.
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-json " JSON"
A JSON value (object, array, string, ...).
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-file " FILE"
Read text from
.IR FILE ;
.B \-
reads stdin.
.PP
States and request documents are capped at 16 MiB. Empty states are
rejected.
.SH OUTPUT
JSON shapes per command are documented in
.IR docs/output.md .
Gate fields
.RB ( threshold ,
.BR pass ,
.BR min_confidence )
are
.B null
when no gate was given. The
.B model
field echoes the resolved model version, not the requested alias.
.B usage
reports billed tokens.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; if a gate was given, it was met.
.TP
.B 1
Gate not met: probability below
.BR \-\-threshold ,
or confidence below
.BR \-\-min\-confidence .
The answer is still printed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage, configuration, IO, or API error. Nothing is printed to stdout.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TYPESAFE_API_KEY
API key (required).
.TP
.B TYPESAFE_DEFAULT_MODEL
Model alias (default:
.BR jev\-latest ).
.TP
.B TYPESAFE_BASE_URL
API root (default:
.BR https://api.typesafe.ai ).
.B Never read from files
\(em real environment only, so a planted file cannot redirect the key to
another host.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.jevcli/jev.conf
User configuration, dotenv-style
.IR KEY=value .
Only
.B TYPESAFE_API_KEY
and
.B TYPESAFE_DEFAULT_MODEL
are honored. Keep it
.BR "chmod 600" ;
a warning is printed when group/other permission bits are set. The
directory should be
.BR "chmod 700" .
.TP
.I ./.env
Project-local environment file; same allowlist.
.PP
Precedence, lowest first:
.I ~/.jevcli/jev.conf
<
.I ./.env
< real environment < CLI flags. Files only fill variables that are not
already set.
.SH EXAMPLES
Gate an action on a probability:
.PP
.nf
.RS
jev\-cli predict \-\-state "$CONTEXT" \e
    \-\-question "Is this change safe to auto\-apply?" \e
    \-\-threshold 0.9 && ./apply.sh
.RE
.fi
.PP
Pick a path and capture the bare answer:
.PP
.nf
.RS
CHOICE=$(jev\-cli choose \-\-format text \-\-state "$CONTEXT" \e
    \-\-question "Which approach is most likely to succeed?" \e
    \-\-option "retry=Retry with backoff" \e
    \-\-option "abort=Stop and ask the user")
.RE
.fi
.PP
Several typed questions in one call:
.PP
.nf
.RS
printf '%s' '{"state": "...", "questions": {
  "ok": {"type": "noul", "instructions": "Will it work?"}
}}' | jev\-cli ask \-
.RE
.fi
.SH SECURITY
.IP \(bu 2
The state is sent verbatim to the TypeSafe API;
.B jev\-cli
does not redact secrets. Keep credentials and sensitive data out of it.
.IP \(bu 2
The API key is only ever sourced from the environment or the two allowlisted
files, is marked sensitive in transport headers, and never appears in
output, logs, or error messages.
.IP \(bu 2
Base URLs must be HTTPS (plain HTTP only for loopback); HTTP redirects are
never followed, so credentials cannot leak cross-origin.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jev\-guard (1)
\(em screening code changes with the same model.
.IR docs/usage.md ,
.IR docs/output.md ,
.I AGENTS.md
in the source distribution.
